WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:07.290
This video is about two things: The first
is SCP – 096, also known as The Shy Guy,

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:12.370
a horrific monster who murders anyone and
anything unfortunate enough to look at its

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:16.530
face, directly or through photos or videos.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:21.860
The second is you – because we asked you
for your favorite questions, theories, and

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.440
hypothetical situations involving 096.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:31.240
We even asked you if you thought someone would
be safe from 096 on the moon, and you delivered.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.510
If you haven’t watched our first video on
the infamous Shy Guy, we recommend checking

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:39.870
that out first, but feel free to stick around
even if you haven’t.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:44.590
First of all, let’s take a look at the questions
you had about the SCP Foundation’s most

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:48.640
dangerous introvert, and see if we can find
some answers.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.860
“How close would you have to be to trigger
it?

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.130
Like, if it was 5km away, would it still count?”

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:58.899
The short answer is that 096’s homicidal
rage can be triggered from pretty much any

00:00:58.899 --> 00:00:59.899
distance.

00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:04.269
We’ll get into some of the potentially crazy
extents of this later on, but if you see the

00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:09.479
Shy Guy’s face while you’re sharing a
dimension with him, you’re in serious trouble.

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:13.749
People who’ve viewed the creature’s face
in different countries, or even miles underwater

00:01:13.749 --> 00:01:19.200
have met gruesome ends 5 kilometers would
definitely not keep you safe.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.389
“What were his origins and how strong is
he compared to SCP-682?”

00:01:24.389 --> 00:01:29.829
The origins of SCP – 096 are still shrouded
in mystery – all we know for sure is that

00:01:29.829 --> 00:01:33.889
he was discovered by the Foundation in a snowy,
mountainous region.

00:01:33.889 --> 00:01:39.749
As for physical durability, he’s about even
with 682 as both survived their encounter.

00:01:39.749 --> 00:01:45.679
We know 682 has the psychological advantage
though, as 096 has been terrified of the lizard

00:01:45.679 --> 00:01:48.179
ever since they met in cross testing.

00:01:48.179 --> 00:01:55.850
However, you could argue that 096 is technically
more dangerous, since unlike 682, 096 has

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.989
never been pacified before killing its intended
target while on a rampage.

00:01:59.989 --> 00:02:05.490
“If he goes into an "unstoppable attack
mode" when someone sees his face, shouldn’t

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:08.179
you NOT show his face in the thumbnail?

00:02:08.179 --> 00:02:13.060
Thankfully, according to the official documents,
artistic representations, like paintings or

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:16.840
digitally-drawn YouTube thumbnails have no
effect.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:22.209
Only actual photographs or videos of the creature
can be deadly, so you’re safe – unless

00:02:22.209 --> 00:02:28.719
we decide to do an 096 Face Reveal to celebrate
our next 100,000 subscribers, of course.

00:02:28.719 --> 00:02:30.629
This leads into our next question.

00:02:30.629 --> 00:02:34.599
“If it attacks you when you look at it,
then how did the scientist draw the picture

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:36.240
of the thing without looking at it?”

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:40.570
That’s a good question, and also one that
occurred to the Foundation scientists, who

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:43.600
came up with an extremely elaborate solution.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:48.599
They put a D-Class tattoo artist inside a
diving bell miles underwater, and had him

00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:52.310
unseal a photograph of the creature before
drawing a copy.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:57.939
This copy was then released from the diving
bell in a sealed container, before 096 inevitably

00:02:57.939 --> 00:02:59.090
got to the poor D-Class.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:05.069
“Does the shy guy have to be viewed through
a good quality image to enter a rage state?”

00:03:05.069 --> 00:03:11.599
Unfortunately no, even the most poorly rendered
or miniscule image of 096’s face is a death

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:12.599
sentence.

00:03:12.599 --> 00:03:16.969
One of the most infamous incidents resulted
from a man seeing a small dot that was only

00:03:16.969 --> 00:03:20.510
a few pixels wide in a photo from an old ski
trip.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:24.689
This dot was 096, taken from a mile away.

00:03:24.689 --> 00:03:29.560
No true image of 096 is safe, regardless of
size.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:35.239
“In some canons, despite 096 being referred
to as indestructible, the Foundation managed

00:03:35.239 --> 00:03:39.060
to terminate it after many attempts and even
more bureaucracy.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.060
How did they do it?”

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:45.420
While a lot of 096’s body has been blown
away by conventional arms fire, its hyper-tough

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:49.609
skeleton is what has given it such an indestructible
reputation.

00:03:49.609 --> 00:03:54.469
In one tale though, Foundation researchers
actually used this to their advantage, and

00:03:54.469 --> 00:03:59.810
employed the use of the neck-snapping killer
sculpture, SCP-173.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:06.610
After using 173 to damage 096’s bones, powerful
acid was injected into the skeleton, destroying

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.109
it from within.

00:04:08.109 --> 00:04:13.609
Though of course, this isn’t the official
ending of the 096 story, because the SCP Foundation

00:04:13.609 --> 00:04:16.269
doesn’t have a single unifying canon.

00:04:16.269 --> 00:04:17.720
That’s enough questions.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:22.570
Now, it’s time for you to school us – let’s
look at some of your favorite theories about

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.150
the Shy Guy.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:25.150
Starting with…

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:29.260
“I sometimes like to imagine that 096 is
nice, but he can’t control when someone

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:33.310
sees him and after he kills the person he
starts to cry because he didn’t want to

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:34.310
kill them.”

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:39.960
There is actually some evidence to suggest
that SCP – 096 might not want to kill.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:46.500
A great example is its cross test with SCP
– 978, a camera which reveals the deepest

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.780
desires of whoever or whatever is in its photos.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:55.260
The photo it took of 096 showed that it had
completely disappeared from the photo – showing

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:59.500
its deepest desire was just to be invisible
and unseen.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.960
Maybe it wants to disappear because it doesn’t
want to hurt anybody?

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:07.980
“Regarding the Moon question, I think SCP-096
would probably stay in that hostile state

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:12.090
until you came back, at which point it would
promptly rip you to shreds and do whatever

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:17.980
it does to your mutilated corpse”
Based on what we know about prior 096 incidents,

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:19.669
this feels incredibly likely.

00:05:19.669 --> 00:05:24.639
It’s also possible that it might enter its
docile state, before becoming aggressive again

00:05:24.639 --> 00:05:27.090
when you return to its murder range.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:30.060
You really don’t want to find out, either
way.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:34.310
“He can jump to the moon easy, he does squats
in containment all the time.”

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:39.040
While its scrawny physique doesn’t make
it seem like 096 understands the concept of

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:45.150
exercise, there aren’t any cameras in 096’s
cell – so technically, we can’t prove

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.790
it isn’t doing squats to pass the time in
there.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:52.520
“I really doubt a blind person would be
safe from his effect, since 096 has the IQ

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:56.070
of a new born baby, I think he will count
it as looking at him”

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:58.099
This is an interesting theory.

00:05:58.099 --> 00:06:03.259
However, seeing as 096 is able to sense when
people see its face from entire continents

00:06:03.259 --> 00:06:08.789
away, the way it knows if you can see its
face might be a little more psychic in nature.

00:06:08.789 --> 00:06:13.460
Therefore, it’s probable that it wouldn’t
mistakenly kill someone who hasn’t actually

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:16.820
seen its face – such as a person who is
blind.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:20.150
“To deal with him in my opinion… simply
freeze him.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.940
Either in space or the mountains.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:25.430
His body shuts down and when looked at it
will not react correctly.

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:26.639
It is simply asleep.”

00:06:26.639 --> 00:06:32.280
While we don’t know how SCP – 096 would
react to a zero-g environment, for a creature

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.880
that’s always nude, it seems extremely tolerant
to the cold.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:41.330
When it was first found, it was lurking in
icy mountains and a Foundation agent commented

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:46.380
on the fact it wasn’t even shivering, despite
the incredibly low temperatures.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:50.900
But who knows if there’s a temperature out
there that’s too low even for the Shy Guy?

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:54.680
“If someone looks at it in China and it’s
the US, then you get on its back, you’ll

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.430
get a free piggy back ride to China.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.180
It’s a free trip to China, and all it costs
is a human life.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:02.370
That’s my theory”
Technically, it’d be at the cost of two

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:06.449
human lives, unless you wore a diving suit
with plenty of Oxygen.

00:07:06.449 --> 00:07:11.630
096 has proven to be an extremely proficient
swimmer, but you’d have to maintain your

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:15.900
grip across the entire Pacific Ocean while
it journeys to China.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:20.650
In other words, it’s technically possible,
but we here at SCP Explained would rather

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.720
pay for the roundtrip flight.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:23.840
To each their own though.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.849
But that’s enough theories for now.

00:07:25.849 --> 00:07:29.909
Let’s move on to the main event: Hypotheticals.

00:07:29.909 --> 00:07:35.759
You posed some great possible scenarios involving
SCP – 096, so we’re going to see if we

00:07:35.759 --> 00:07:37.379
can find the answers.

00:07:37.379 --> 00:07:41.419
“What would happen if someone looked at
a picture of it while in or before entering

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:44.560
another SCP’s pocket dimension or mirror
dimension?”

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:49.900
There aren’t any canon examples to prove
either way, but if there’s any kind of consistent

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:56.020
entry point into this dimension, it’s likely
that 096 would find a way to follow you in.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:08:01.610
If not, it’s very possible that it may just
wait for you to eventually return, before

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:04.810
bringing the metaphorical hammer down on you.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:09.000
So technically, if you were pulled into the
Old Man’s pocket dimension and he closed

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:14.680
the portal, you’d be safe from 096, but
then you’ve got a whole other problem to

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:15.680
deal with.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:20.370
“What happens if a person sees his face
then gets their memory of the creature wiped?”

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:24.460
Considering how good the Foundation seems
to be at wiping people’s memories and their

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:29.689
access to amnestics, if this worked, they
probably would have made it standard procedure

00:08:29.689 --> 00:08:31.430
by now – so it’s unlikely.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:35.710
“What happens if a person looked at it and
the person then went on a plane?

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:38.570
Or just staying in the air or space what would
it do?”

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:44.330
096 has shown the ability to jump up and destroy
low-flying aircraft, but otherwise, it’s

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:48.750
likely that the creature would probably run
to a point directly below you and remain there

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.820
until you touched back down.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:55.140
Since you’ll need food and water at some
point and aircrafts need fuel, you’d probably

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:57.230
just be prolonging the inevitable.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:02.090
“What if the young girl was around it so
it tried to attack her but died trying?”

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:04.760
This is another interesting possibility.

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:11.380
SCP-053 is a girl capable of causing homicidal
urges, but causes fatal heart attacks in those

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:12.560
who attack her.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:18.580
While we can’t know for sure how a meeting
between 096 and 053 would go, we can use her

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:22.220
encounter with 682 as a potential template.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:26.600
Aggressive SCPs like the hard to kill reptile,
perhaps having an innate knowledge of the

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:32.570
danger that comes from attacking 053, tend
to become strangely docile around her.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:36.000
It’s possible that 096 would do the same.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:41.150
“Would we be able to control SCP-096 with
the help of SCP-035?”

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:50.290
The Possessive Mask, aka SCP – 035, is undeniably
a lot more intelligent than 096, and has even

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:53.090
been shown to respond to reason on occasion.

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:57.740
It’s also been able to control almost every
other entity it’s been placed on.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:04.020
The problem is, if the Mask was placed on
096, and it was somehow effective, the result

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:10.000
may be even more dangerous than 096 – An
intelligent monster with an indestructible

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.000
and highly dangerous body.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.800
There’s no telling whether 035 would slowly
break down 096 into sludge the way it does

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:24.410
to humans, in which case we could be left
with an immortal 096 - 035 combo.

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:27.050
So maybe it’s best that we never find out.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:31.490
“If someone were to be in the infinite Ikea,
and looked at a picture of its face, could

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:36.070
it be finally contained, and if someone else
looked at a picture of it outside of the Infinite

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:40.530
Ikea, could it escape and kill them, if so,
how long would it take it?”

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:47.590
This is a great question, and while the infinite
Ikea is a terrifying maze, SCP -096 has an

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:52.440
advantage here that we don’t: Not only can
it rip through anything in the way with its

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:57.270
super strength, it has an innate sense of
where its victim is.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:03.970
Therefore, regardless of whether you’re
inside and out, SCP -096 will still come straight

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:07.200
to you to exact your horrible fate.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:10.710
But at least you can enjoy the meatballs while
you wait, right?

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:11.710
And finally:

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:16.650
“What would happen if 096 were led into
a room full of mirrors and allowed or made

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:18.560
to look at its own face?

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.920
Would it smash the mirrors or try to rip itself
to pieces?”

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:27.160
This is still a hotly debated issue to this
day, which – thanks to the “no canon”

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:31.900
nature of the SCP Foundation – doesn’t
have a definitive answer.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:37.760
Some theorize that this would at least be
an effective deterrent against SCP – 096,

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:42.280
while others suggest that it wouldn’t be
effective, because many believe that 096 is

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:46.050
actually blind and thus cannot see its own
face.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:49.110
It can only sense when other people see it.

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:54.330
Again, we don’t quite know for sure, but
it’s likely to remain one of the most contentious

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:58.380
issues around the Shy Guy for a long time
to come.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:02.850
And there you have it, folks, our very first
questions and theories video.

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:07.220
We loved hearing what you had to say, so keep
an eye on our community posts for the next

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:08.220
one!

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:12.000
Are there other SCPs you’d like to see us
cover in Explained or Theory videos?

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.740
Let us know in the comments!

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:20.010
And subscribe to SCP Explained and turn on
notifications for new SCP Videos every single

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.010
week!

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:27.200
And while you’re here, go check out “SCP
– 053 – The Young Girl” and “SCP – 682

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:32.780
– Ways The Foundation Tried To Kill The
Hard To Destroy Reptile” for more SCP Foundation

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:33.580
classics!

